{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (DOCTOR): Come through. What's going on?",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Headaches. I've had them for years, but they're different and I'm sick of it.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (DOCTOR): Different how?",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (PATIENT): Worse when I wake up. And I'm throwing up with them now, which I never did.",
  "[SEG0005] person_1 (DOCTOR): How long have the morning ones been happening?",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (PATIENT): Um, three weeks? Maybe a bit more. I don't know. Work's been mad.",
  "[SEG0007] person_1 (DOCTOR): The old ones, how long?",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (PATIENT): Five-ish years. On and off. Someone called them migraines.",
  "[SEG0009] person_1 (DOCTOR): Which side?",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (PATIENT): Left. Throbbing. Most days lately, which is just great.",
  "[SEG0011] person_1 (DOCTOR): Do you get flashing lights before the pain?",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (PATIENT): I'm not weak anywhere, if that's what you're getting at. And I already said I vomit in the mornings.",
  "[SEG0013] person_1 (DOCTOR): I asked about your vision. Flashing lights or blurred vision, yes or no?",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (PATIENT): No. No flashing lights, and nothing blurry.",
  "[SEG0015] person_1 (DOCTOR): What do you take for them?",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (PATIENT): Sumatriptan, and heaps of Panadol.",
  "[SEG0017] person_1 (DOCTOR): What strength is the sumatriptan?",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (PATIENT): Fifty milligrams, I think. Tablets. One when the headache starts.",
  "[SEG0019] person_1 (DOCTOR): How many days a week are you taking it?",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (PATIENT): Most days these last few weeks on the sumatriptan. It was two or three times a week before that, for ages. And my partner keeps saying I snore and I'm knackered all the time, which is rubbish.",
  "[SEG0021] person_1 (DOCTOR): So are you tired in the daytime?",
  "[SEG0022] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah, I'm tired, because I sleep badly and work won't let up. I do not snore.",
  "[SEG0023] person_1 (DOCTOR): How much Panadol?",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (PATIENT): A gram, two tablets, for the head. Sometimes four times a day if it's really going.",
  "[SEG0025] person_1 (DOCTOR): Neck stiffness?",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0027] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any fever?",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0029] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any fits or blackouts?",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (PATIENT): No. Obviously.",
  "[SEG0031] person_1 (DOCTOR): Anything else in your history, apart from the migraines?",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (PATIENT): No. Just this.",
  "[SEG0033] person_1 (DOCTOR): Blood pressure is one thirty-eight over eighty-six. Pulse seventy-four.",
  "[SEG0034] person_2 (PATIENT): So?",
  "[SEG0035] person_1 (DOCTOR): That's all right. Pupils are equal and reactive. No papilloedema.",
  "[SEG0036] person_2 (PATIENT): Can you not shine that thing, my head's killing me.",
  "[SEG0037] person_1 (DOCTOR): Arms up. Power is normal, no drift. Legs are strong, gait is steady.",
  "[SEG0038] person_2 (PATIENT): I told you I'm not weak.",
  "[SEG0039] person_1 (DOCTOR): Working impression is medication overuse headache on top of migraine, from the near-daily sumatriptan and Panadol.",
  "[SEG0040] person_2 (PATIENT): Brilliant. So it's my fault.",
  "[SEG0041] person_1 (DOCTOR): I didn't say fault. I also can't exclude an intracranial cause while you're vomiting in the mornings.",
  "[SEG0042] person_2 (PATIENT): You think it's a brain tumour.",
  "[SEG0043] person_1 (DOCTOR): I didn't say that. If the morning headache and vomiting haven't settled in a fortnight, we'll organise a CT of the head.",
  "[SEG0044] person_2 (PATIENT): Not now?",
  "[SEG0045] person_1 (DOCTOR): Not now. If it's no better in a fortnight, come back and see me. Sudden worst headache, new weakness, or you can't stay awake, go straight to emergency. And ease off, don't take the sumatriptan more than a couple of days a week, and cut the daily Panadol."
 ],
